{{- /*
  support/channel-fragment-read — inline ONE topical fragment of the per-channel
  support playbook AT RENDER TIME.

  Fragments live under `.mitto/support/<channel-id>/<fragment>.md`, one topic
  per file. Standard fragments: scope, tone, investigation, resources,
  escalation, redirects.

  Architectural intent (mitto-eyf): the fragment CONTENT is embedded verbatim
  into the rendered prompt via Go text/template — the agent never reads the
  file at runtime. This makes prompts auditable (the exact bytes the agent
  received are visible in event logs), deterministic (no per-run filesystem
  drift), and cheaper (no shell/tool round-trip).

  When the fragment file is MISSING, the template falls back to a short
  `[CONTEXT]` note or an owner-ask instruction, depending on `OwnerAsk`.

  Callers pass named fields via a `dict`:

      Channel:  the Slack channel id (e.g. C0XXXXXXX). Required. Callers that
                do not know the channel at render time (per-bead prompts that
                receive only IssueID) should pass "" — the template then emits
                a minimal runtime-read instruction as a last-resort fallback,
                so the caller still gets fragment content.
      Fragment: short filename stem (no extension). One of:
                "scope" | "tone" | "investigation" | "resources"
                | "escalation" | "redirects".
      Purpose:  short caller-supplied phrase spliced into "use it to <Purpose>".
      Owner:    canonical name of the owner prompt, e.g. "Support: reply to
                user" — used in the missing-file / no-channel message so the
                reader tells the user which prompt would populate it. Required.
      OwnerAsk: bool. If true, the CALLING prompt is itself the owner and
                should ask + write when the fragment is missing. If false
                (reader mode), the caller just logs a `[CONTEXT]` note and
                continues with in-prompt defaults.

  Usage (rendered as a single Markdown bullet — the CALLER supplies the
  leading `- `):

      - {{ template "_shared/support/channel-fragment-read"
           (dict "Channel"  $channel
                 "Fragment" "tone"
                 "Purpose"  "shape the tone when drafting the reply"
                 "Owner"    "Support: reply to user"
                 "OwnerAsk" false) }}
*/ -}}
{{- $channel := .Channel -}}
{{- $fragment := .Fragment -}}
{{- $purpose  := .Purpose  -}}
{{- $owner    := .Owner    -}}
{{- $ownerAsk := .OwnerAsk -}}
{{- $path := printf ".mitto/support/%s/%s.md" $channel $fragment -}}
{{- if and $channel (FileExists $path) -}}
**Channel `{{ $fragment }}` (embedded from `{{ $path }}`)** — this is the
authoritative `{{ $fragment }}` guide for channel `{{ $channel }}`; use it to
{{ $purpose }}. It **overrides** the generic defaults in the caller prompt.

<!-- BEGIN {{ $path }} -->
{{ ReadFile $path }}
<!-- END {{ $path }} -->
{{- else if $channel -}}
**Channel `{{ $fragment }}` fragment MISSING** (`{{ $path }}` does not exist for channel
`{{ $channel }}`).
{{- if $ownerAsk }} This prompt owns creating it: ask the user for the `{{ $fragment }}`
content via a focused `mitto_ui_form`, write the file, then proceed. See the owner-ask
step below for the field list.
{{- else }} Log a short `[CONTEXT]` bead comment noting `{{ $fragment }}.md missing —
using generic defaults; owner = **{{ $owner }}**` and continue with the generic defaults
in this section. Do **not** ask the user here — only **{{ $owner }}** is responsible
for populating this fragment.
{{- end }}
{{- else -}}
**Channel `{{ $fragment }}` fragment (runtime read fallback)** — the caller did not
supply a channel id at render time, so this fragment could not be inlined. Using the
bead's `slack_channel` value, read
**`.mitto/support/<channel-id>/{{ $fragment }}.md`** (e.g. `C0XXXXXXX` →
`.mitto/support/C0XXXXXXX/{{ $fragment }}.md`). This is the authoritative
`{{ $fragment }}` guide for this channel — use it to {{ $purpose }}. **If it exists**,
honor its guidance; it **overrides** the generic defaults below.
{{- if $ownerAsk }} **If it does not exist**, this prompt owns creating it: ask the user
for the `{{ $fragment }}` content via a focused `mitto_ui_form`, write the file, then
proceed. See the owner-ask step below for the field list.
{{- else }} **If it does not exist**, log a short `[CONTEXT]` bead comment noting
`{{ $fragment }}.md missing — using generic defaults; owner = **{{ $owner }}**` and
continue with the generic defaults in this section. Do **not** ask the user here — only
**{{ $owner }}** is responsible for populating this fragment.
{{- end }}
{{- end -}}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
